# Dart style

- Prefer `final` locals and `const` widgets where values are fixed at compile time.
- Contracts: `abstract interface class XRepository` (not a concrete base class to extend).
- Prefer composition (inject dependencies, small widgets) over deep inheritance.
- One reason to change per type; split files when presentation and domain mix.
- Comments: follow `comments.mdc` (minimal; no narrating the obvious).

```dart
// BAD
class EngineRepositoryImpl extends EngineRepository { ... }

// GOOD — see lib/features/recording/domain/repositories/engine_repository.dart
abstract interface class EngineRepository {
  Future<EngineInfo> getEngineInfo();
}
```

- Follow `analysis_options.yaml` (strict casts, `prefer_single_quotes`, no `print`).
- Generated files (`*.g.dart`): do not hand-edit.